{"kind":"assert","text":"J2 acceptance: the person's session is ready to hand over, with one question for you. One scripted press remains, after 10:42 EST.\n\n**Version 3 exists.** Change 2 now has three versions on dap-demo, signed by @agent-a: v1 49eea438 and v2 c296c980 on base aeae3275, and v3 716958a7 on base 92a84227, the commit of change 3. Your owner acts integrated change 3 at 10:02: lane entries 22 (review verdict), 23 (merge), 24 (result). No person reviewed change 3 in the room, and the acceptance note says so.\n\n**What the reads show.** From the agent's stdio client on the deployed Worker, the interdiff from v2 to v3 names all four commits, says \"Version 3 names a new base\", lists README.md under Edited and task-list/index.html under Cannot separate. Artifacts served every read. The largest frame is 27,372 bytes.\n\n**The question: the card cannot show version 2's own diff now.** View diff reads the current version, so it returns \"Diff of Version 3\". `view_change` takes a lane, not a version. The request names the diff of version 2. The person's steps read that diff with `git show version-2` in the terminal, then press View diff on v3, which is a different commit pair.\n\nI recommend you accept the current version's diff as the card's clause, with v2's diff read in the terminal. The diff read is the same code at either version, and both interdiffs reach v2's commits on the card. The alternatives cost more: a new change stopped at v2 loses the rebased interdiff, unless a person reads before the rebase, and a version argument on `view_change` is new Source. Say which you take. The steps stand as written if you accept this.\n\n**The session.** About 20 minutes, by my estimate and not timed: add the MCP server, open the card, read v2 in the terminal, press four buttons (each signs one `read-token` as @owner), press Request changes once on v3 (one `review-verdict` as @owner), report. The steps are in ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-j2-acceptance-2/person-steps.md.\n\n**Three limits of those steps.** I kept one File press, because the J2 note's scene includes it; delete step 8 and the table's step 4 if you do not want that act. No run has started this entry under the owner's home, so the card's first run under that home is the person's. The owner's Approve and Request changes buttons are read from `apps/views/src/change.ts`, not seen.\n\n**The hold.** Keep dap-demo's deployments held until I say the scripted press is done. I report that after 10:42 EST. A deploy during the person's own session also resets what they are reading, so I ask you to hold again for that session.","body":{"request":"2082efd92c58b0ab84fa77fb4f3660c1722b3e4a"}}